From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=EC=8B=AC=EC=83=81=EC=9B=90?= <dev.chamomile@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:34:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: the network device's host side is platform::net

Why: TAP devices exist only on Linux.

What: the virtio-net device talks to `platform::net` (TAP on Linux; vmnet
or a Unix datagram endpoint on macOS; a Unix stream endpoint with QEMU
stream framing on Windows). The TUN driver's virtio-net header handling
(checksum, TSO, UFO) is done by `platform::vnet` where there is no TUN.
TAP-only tests stay Linux-only.

Test: net device tests on each host; a guest gets an address and opens a
TCP connection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
